                          </note>
                        </item>

                        <item xml:id="a3">
                           <desc type="CommemorativeNote"/>
                           <locus from="107r" to="107v"/>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ኦእግዚኦ፡ አዕረፍ፡ ነፍሳተ፡ አበዊነ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="PRS9602Turaev"/>
                           </q>
                           <q xml:lang="en">Oh Lord, let the souls of our fathers rest in peace ... </q>
                        </item>

                        <item xml:id="a4">
                          <locus from="108r" to="116v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2722RepCh6">Malkǝʾa śǝqāyu la-Giyorgis</title></desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"><lb n="1"/>መልክዓ፡ ሥቃይ፡ ስኡላነ፡ መጽሔት፡ ሥጋከ፡ አርአየ፡
                      <lb n="2"/> እምአመ፡ ትቤ፡ ላዕለከ፡ እስከ፡ ፈጸምከ፡ ሥቃየ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="PRS9602Turaev"/>
                           </q>
                           <note>In this manuscript the hymn encompasses 43 strophes.</note>
                        </item>

                        <item xml:id="a5">
                           <locus from="116r" to="117v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2769RepCh53">Malkǝʾ-hymn to Takla Hāymānot</title></desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"><lb n="1"/>ሰላም፡ ለከ፡ ተክለ፡ ሃይማኖት፡ ምሉዕ፡ ሞገስ፡ ወጸጋ፡
                    <lb n="2"/> ስፉሕ፡ አዕጹቅ፡ ወይን፡ እንበለ፡ ንትጋ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="PRS9602Turaev"/>
                           </q>
                           <note>The excerpt from the hymn encompasses 11 strophes.</note>
                        </item>

                        <item xml:id="a6">
                           <locus from="118r" to="120v"/>
                            <desc type="GuestText"><title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2915RepCh196">Malkǝʾa Gabra Manfas Qǝddus</title></desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"><lb n="1"/>ሰላም፡ ለጽንሰትከ፡ መሰረተ፡ ነገር፡ ወውጣኔ፡<gap reason="ellipsis" resp="PRS9602Turaev"/>
                           </q>
                           <note>The excerpt from the hymn encompasses 17 strophes.</note>
                        </item>

                        <item xml:id="a7">
                           <locus target="#121r"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">
                           <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT5780Orationes12">Protective ʾasmāt-prayer</title></desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">በስመ፡ አብ፡ ወወልድ፡ ወመንፈስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ፩አምላክ፡ በጢት፡ ስመከ፡
                      በጥጥያብ፡ ስምከ፡ በቆፍ፡ ስምከ፡ በቀያፋ፡ ስምከ፡ በሰይፍ፡ ስምከ፡ በስስያብ፡ ስምከ፡ ዘአብራህከ፡
                      ዓይኖ፡ ለጢሜዎስ፡ ወልደ፡ በርጢሜዎስ፡ ዕውር፡ ከማሁ፡ አብራህ፡ አይኖ፡ ለገብርከ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="PRS9602Turaev"/>
                      ያሸላል፡ ያሸላትያል፡ ዘበቃልከ፡ ወበዘስምከ፡ ድማኅ፡ አደኅኖ፡ ለገብርከ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="PRS9602Turaev"/>
                           እግዚአብሔር፡ ብርሃን፡ በእንተ፡ ማእሰሩ፡ ለሰይጣን፡ ዘስሙ፡ አስማተ፡ ኃያላን፡ ሰፒራ፡</q>
                           <bibl>
                                <ptr target="bm:Turaev1899Orationes"/>
                                <citedRange unit="page">249-250</citedRange>
                             </bibl>
                             <bibl>
                                <ptr target="bm:Turaev1899Orationes"/>
                                <citedRange unit="number">12</citedRange>
                             </bibl>
                           </item>

                        <item xml:id="a8">
                           <locus from="118r" to="120v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2915RepCh196">Malkǝʾa Gabra Manfas Qǝddus</title></desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"><lb n="1"/>ሰላም፡ ለጽንሰትከ፡ መሰረተ፡ ነገር፡ ወውጣኔ፡
                    <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="PRS9602Turaev"/></q>
                           <note>The excerpt from the hymn encompasses 17 strophes.</note>
                        </item>
